# Anti Failed Rollback Concern

## Scope
Ensure stock rollback always succeeds using atomic transactions - if rollback fails, system must retry or alert, never leave stock in reserved state indefinitely.

## Out of Scope
Complex rollback strategies, manual retry intervention, rollback persistence beyond atomic transaction.

# Aftermath target
After completion: atomic transaction wrapping reserve and rollback operations, rollback failure detection with retry logic, rollback failure alerting. No stock left in reserved state after failed rollback.

## Definition of Done
[ ] Atomic transaction: wrap reserve and rollback in single transaction
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Transaction started', { requestId })` before reserve
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Transaction committed', { requestId })` after success
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Transaction rolled back', { requestId })` after rollback
    [ ] Test: Reserve stock, verify transaction atomic (all succeed or all fail)
[ ] Rollback failure detection: detect and retry failed rollbacks
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Rollback failed', { requestId, error })` on rollback failure
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Rollback retry', { requestId, attempt })` on retry
    [ ] Test: Simulate rollback failure, verify retry triggered
[ ] Rollback alerting: alert if rollback fails after retries
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Rollback failed permanently', { requestId, error })` after final failure
    [ ] Test: Fail rollback repeatedly, verify alert logged
